k compensation."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $4.5B (43% of market cap)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 12.4% over 3 years, 18.5% over 5 years and 12.3% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 18%).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 29%.","Capex runs only 0.5x depreciation (0.2% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 17, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.4%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (5 sales, net $4.1M sold).","It returns 9.7% a year to shareholders (9.7% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 2.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 19,000 employees, each generates about $2.4M of revenue, 6.4x the Healthcare median, and revenue has grown 16.8% a year across its filed history.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$33K per employee.","CEO pay is $2.1M (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (8/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":74,"head":"Watch: FCF margin 1.4% (burns cash).","pros":["Trades 38% below fair value of $319","Revenue grew 18.5%/yr over 5y","Net cash of $4.5B","Altman Z in the safe zone","P/E 20.5x vs sector 25.8x"],"cons":["FCF margin 1.4% (burns cash)"],"flags":[],"need":["its composite (36) is below 39"],"buy_below":271.13,"vc":{"base":318.98,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":318.98,"n_alt":2,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.664,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (66% dispersion)"]},"med":{"pe":25.8408,"ev_ebitda":15.264,"pfcf":22.3287,"pb":3.2427,"roic":-0.1379,"gross_margin":0.5557,"fcf_margin":0.0222,"div_yield":0.014}},"ticker":"MOH","date":"2026-11-20"}